                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7616b041-f39b-316e-b6e3-d9b0eba5ad10",
                        "entry_id": "c5cf78eb-ff38-30dd-be4a-26cc8463e71e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who drivels."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd9d47d1-93d0-47ce-b8ec-bc5afb1e8a05",
                                "sense_id": "7616b041-f39b-316e-b6e3-d9b0eba5ad10",
                                "text": "I can smash Shakspeare; I can prove Milton to be a driveller, or the contrary: but, for preference, take, as I have said, the abusive line."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f98cb06-c0be-4851-9e58-aa04fc409b66",
                                "sense_id": "7616b041-f39b-316e-b6e3-d9b0eba5ad10",
                                "text": "Think of the men whom I may call book-eaters! Dr. Parr was a driveller; Porson was a sort of learned pig who routed up truffles in the classic garden; poor Buckle became, through stress of books, a shallow thinker; Mezzofanti, with his sixty-four languages and dialects, was perilously like a fool; and more than one modern professor may be counted as nothing else but a vain, over-educated boor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d499795d-6742-4ebd-ac55-9dad099fa01f",
                                "sense_id": "7616b041-f39b-316e-b6e3-d9b0eba5ad10",
                                "text": "[416:6] What intelligent Christian can believe that a minister, instructed by Paul or Peter, and filling one of the most important stations in the apostolic Church, was verily such an ignorant driveller?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a6e06ae-8925-43ef-9bcc-7b8297f36e10",
                                "sense_id": "7616b041-f39b-316e-b6e3-d9b0eba5ad10",
                                "text": "\"All able men,\" adds Macaulay, \"ridiculed him as a dunce, a driveller, a child who never knew his own mind an hour together; and yet he overreached them all.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e41f67cd-6242-4aeb-acb2-0a287bfa0229",
                                "sense_id": "7616b041-f39b-316e-b6e3-d9b0eba5ad10",
                                "text": "And, to leave this miserable driveller without a pretence for his cowardice, the Prince asks it as a personal favour of me, forsooth, not to press my just and reasonable request at this moment."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d86b9e26-de6a-3728-ad42-0fb21357f5c4",
                        "entry_id": "c5cf78eb-ff38-30dd-be4a-26cc8463e71e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The pole used to launch the beer-soaked cloth in the game of dwile flonking."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46f8ef51-0bf1-4ba6-9ce6-26bedf866d1d",
                                "sense_id": "d86b9e26-de6a-3728-ad42-0fb21357f5c4",
                                "text": "Well away from the centre of sanity is dwile flonking. In this game, or possibly sport, a circle of girters dances round a member of the opposing team who revolves in the opposite direction holding a driveller."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
